      "message": "This function is not actually safe by Rust standards. I mean, it takes a pointer and writes to it. Also there\u0027s a safety requirement that the buffer is a valid buffer.\n\nI think your handwritten Rust wrapper needs to be marked `unsafe`. Additionally, we don\u0027t actually want a handwritten Rust wrapper anyway. The aim is to ultimately use the automatic inlines.\n\n(Also, existing issue, but you cannot use `as_ptr()` with any C FFI. See https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl/+/HEAD/API-CONVENTIONS.md#pointers-and-slices and https://davidben.net/2024/01/15/empty-slices.html)",
